    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "tangible progress feels like a joke when u realize how much time u wasted. like i've spent years obsessed with being \"great\" and now i'm just staring at a career that's basically just maintenance. it's not that i'm unhappy with the work, it's just that the whole existence of being \"just okay\" feels like a slow death. it's hollow.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
